5:["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg text-white/70 max-w-xl mx-auto mb-6","children":"From toddlers to over-70s, the recommended frequency of eye tests varies by age, health, and risk factors. Learn exactly when to book your next appointment."}]
6:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-sm text-white/50","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5","children":[["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-4 h-4","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.25M3 18.75V7.5a2.25 2.25 0 012.25-2.25h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 7.5v11.25m-18 0A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75m-18 0v-7.5A2.25 2.25 0 015.25 9h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 11.25v7.5"}]}],"18 November 2025"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"w-px h-3.5 bg-white/20"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5","children":[["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-4 h-4","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M12 6v6h4.5m4.5 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"}]}],"7 min read"]}]]}]
7:["$","section",null,{"className":"py-12 sm:py-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-[16/9] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-8","children":["$","$Ld",null,{"src":"/images/optician-shop-sm.jpg","alt":"How Often Should You Have an Eye Test? — Age-by-Age Advice","fill":true,"sizes":"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 66vw","className":"object-cover","priority":true}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"prose prose-gray max-w-none","children":[["$","h2","0",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mt-10 mb-4","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"Why regular eye tests matter"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"Regular eye tests are one of the most important yet frequently overlooked aspects of preventive healthcare in the UK. Unlike many other medical assessments, an eye examination does far more than simply check whether you need glasses. A comprehensive eye test can detect the early signs of serious systemic conditions such as diabetes, high blood pressure, high cholesterol, and even brain tumours, often before you experience any symptoms at all. The back of the eye is the only place in the body where blood vessels can be observed directly without surgery, making it a uniquely valuable diagnostic window."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"Despite these benefits, research consistently shows that millions of British adults are overdue for an eye test. A 2024 survey by the Association of Optometrists found that roughly one in four UK adults had not visited an optician in the past two years, and many could not remember the last time they had their eyes examined. This is concerning because conditions such as glaucoma, age-related macular degeneration, and diabetic retinopathy can progress silently, causing irreversible damage before symptoms become noticeable."}],["$","p","3",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"The good news is that knowing how often you should have an eye test is straightforward, once you understand the general guidelines and the personal risk factors that might mean you need more frequent checks. In this guide, we break down the recommendations by age group, outline who qualifies for free NHS eye tests, and highlight the warning signs that should prompt an immediate visit to your optician."}],["$","h2","4",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mt-10 mb-4","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"General guidelines for adults"}],["$","p","5",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"For most healthy adults aged 18 to 69, the standard recommendation is to have a comprehensive eye test every two years. This biennial schedule is endorsed by the College of Optometrists and the NHS, and it strikes a sensible balance between catching early problems and minimising unnecessary appointments. During a routine eye test, your optician will check your visual acuity, assess the health of your eyes using specialised equipment, and screen for conditions like glaucoma and cataracts."}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"However, the two-year guideline is a minimum, not a maximum. If you notice any changes in your vision between appointments, such as blurriness, difficulty reading, headaches, or seeing flashing lights and floaters, you should book an eye test straight away rather than waiting for your next scheduled visit. Your optician may also recommend more frequent visits based on your individual circumstances, family history, or the results of your last examination."}],"$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22"]}]]}],"$L23"]}]}]}]
8:["$","section",null,{"className":"py-16 sm:py-20 bg-gray-50","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-center mb-12","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mb-3","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"More articles"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-500 max-w-lg mx-auto","children":"Continue reading our expert guides on eye tests and eye health"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 lg:gap-8","children":[["$","$L3","what-happens-during-an-eye-test",{"href":"/articles/what-happens-during-an-eye-test","className":"group card-lift flex flex-col bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm overflow-hidden h-full","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-[16/10] img-zoom","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"src":"/images/eye-test-phoropter-sm.jpg","alt":"What Happens During an Eye Test? A Step-by-Step Guide","fill":true,"sizes":"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 33vw","className":"object-cover"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-3 left-3 text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full backdrop-blur-sm bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700","children":"Guides"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col flex-1 p-5 sm:p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] group-hover:text-[var(--color-primary)] transition-colors mb-2 line-clamp-2","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"What Happens During an Eye Test? A Step-by-Step Guide"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4 line-clamp-3","children":"Nervous about your eye test? Walk through every stage of a modern UK eye examination, from the history questions to the final prescription."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-auto flex items-center justify-between","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-gray-400","children":"8 min read"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-primary)] group-hover:gap-2 transition-all","children":["Read more",["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-4 h-4","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M9 5l7 7-7 7"}]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","$L3","signs-you-need-an-eye-test",{"href":"/articles/signs-you-need-an-eye-test","className":"group card-lift flex flex-col bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm overflow-hidden h-full","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-[16/10] img-zoom","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"src":"/images/oct-scan-sm.jpg","alt":"10 Signs You Need an Eye Test","fill":true,"sizes":"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 33vw","className":"object-cover"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-3 left-3 text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full backdrop-blur-sm bg-[var(--color-primary)]/10 text-[var(--color-primary)]","children":"Eye Health"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col flex-1 p-5 sm:p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] group-hover:text-[var(--color-primary)] transition-colors mb-2 line-clamp-2","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"10 Signs You Need an Eye Test"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4 line-clamp-3","children":"Headaches, squinting, and holding your phone at arm's length? Discover the key warning signs that it's time to visit your optician."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-auto flex items-center justify-between","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-gray-400","children":"6 min read"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-primary)] group